            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 68-year-old male, admitted on 11/04/2011 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure, chest X-ray showing hyperinflation without consolidation, and blood tests revealing mild inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout the stay. Treatment consisted of controlled oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 12/04/2011 with a tapering oral steroid course and optimised inhaler regimen. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me with any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
